{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"r1","type":"claim","text":"The recurring we-disagree-what-the-agreement-meant fights are better modelled as collisions of diverging private ledgers than as under-specification: people systematically over-credit their own contributions, so each flatmate's sense of what is owed is anchored to a tally the others cannot see.","grounds":"Studies of couples find that partners' estimates of their respective shares of household chores sum to well over 100 percent, consistent with availability-based self-credit.","bearing":"Reframes meaning-disputes as ledger grievances surfaced in contract language."},{"id":"r2","type":"claim","text":"Because ledger divergence persists even under clear wording, the achievable design goal is cheap, bounded disagreement rather than unambiguous agreement; treating near-zero disputes as attainable makes a normally functioning system look like a failure.","depends":["r1"]},{"id":"r3","type":"claim","text":"The friend's avoidance is consistent with a standing problem, not only process-fatigue: in a three-person household, talks that reliably end with the same person assigned or outvoted make attendance a predictable defeat, so opting out is rational. Whether the asker and the other friend form a de facto bloc is undetermined by the available material.","bearing":"Sets sequencing: standing diagnosis before mechanism design."},{"id":"r4","type":"claim","text":"Convening and administering any fix is itself unpaid coordination labour — a fourth chore. If the asker becomes permanent house manager, the role will attract resentment and may be precisely what the avoider is withdrawing from."},{"id":"r5","type":"objection","text":"Against the system-design-first sequencing of the selected account (h005.fork5.p.rival.0), which leads with written agreements and a weekly re-deal: those remedies presuppose exactly the willing participation that the account's own third fault declares absent, so the repair opens on its strongest ground and leaves the least repairable fault for last. The objection is to the order of operations, not to the mechanisms themselves; because the selected account's commitment field is not exposed, this objection is targeted at its body-level approach in prose rather than at a citable record.","bearing":"If the standing fault is real, the written-system remedies are unusable until it is addressed; if it is not, the objection lapses."},{"id":"r6","type":"commitment","scope":"Weekly allocation of chores","action":"Replace consensus negotiation with rotating proposer/veto: one flatmate per week, on rotation with the avoider scheduled early, publishes a written draft allocation against the actual work rosters; the others may veto the whole draft but not amend it line by line; a veto triggers a published default such as repeating last week's rota. Trial for four weeks.","consequence":"Shrinks meetings to yes/no decisions, gives the avoidant flatmate turns of control rather than of obligation, and retains a written record as the proposer's draft."},{"id":"r7","type":"commitment","scope":"Standards","action":"Set the house standard deliberately at the level all three actually accept; any cleanliness beyond it is owned by whoever wants it — their labour or their money, with no conscription of lower-standard flatmates.","consequence":"Ends taxation-by-taste and legitimises an explicit, shared lower standard.","grounds":"Much recurring conflict is a standards gap rather than an allocation gap."},{"id":"r8","type":"commitment","scope":"Disputes over what past agreements meant","action":"Adopt a bounded dispute protocol: each meaning-dispute receives one airing at a fixed ten-minute weekly slot; if unresolved in a single round, settle by alternation (whoever lost the previous dispute wins this one) and bar reopening.","consequence":"Makes re-litigating wording costlier than conceding; accepts crude fairness as the price of ending trench warfare.","depends":["r2"]},{"id":"r9","type":"commitment","scope":"Outsourcing","action":"Obtain one cleaner quote and keep it standing on the table: any chore still contested after two weekly cycles gets outsourced with the cost split three ways.","consequence":"Makes the price of conflict visible and removes the most-contested items (bathroom, floors) from the dispute surface entirely."},{"id":"r10","type":"commitment","scope":"Sequencing and diagnosis","action":"Before proposing any mechanism, hold separate private conversations: ask each friend what a fair week looks like, and ask the avoidant friend directly whether the talks feel fair and whether they have a real say; compare the three answers to measure the standards gap and test for a two-against-one dynamic. Then offer the mechanisms as a menu and let the avoider choose among them — the choosing is the re-engagement.","consequence":"Any redesign that follows rests on observed answers rather than on speculation, including this account's own.","depends":["r3"]},{"id":"r11","type":"objection","target":["r9"],"text":"Priced and market-flavoured mechanisms presume flatmates who read chores as allocations; flatmates who read chores as care may experience a standing cleaner quote, ill-timed, as an insult to the household.","bearing":"Demotes r9 from standing fixture to negotiable option: it should be offered, not installed."},{"id":"r12","type":"commitment","scope":"Alternative allocation structure","action":"If veto rates under the proposer mechanism run high, fall back to whole-domain ownership with quarterly rotation: each flatmate owns a defined domain end-to-end, sovereign over methods and standards within it.","consequence":"Eliminates week-to-week negotiation almost entirely at the cost of coarser fairness."},{"id":"r13","type":"objection","target":["r12"],"text":"Domains differ in load, so fixed ownership entrenches inequality.","bearing":"Mitigated by quarterly rotation and periodic re-weighting of domains; reduces but does not eliminate the defect."},{"id":"r14","type":"problem","text":"How can the asker run the private standing-check (r10) without the separate conversations themselves reading as coalition-building or a reconvened ambush to the avoidant friend?","depends":["r10"]},{"id":"r15","type":"problem","text":"If the avoidant friend's disengagement predates the chore fights — relationship drift or an intention to move out — no chore mechanism will hold their engagement, and the open question becomes whether the household should be continued rather than reorganised."}],"uptake":["r1","r2","r3","r4","r5","r6","r7","r8","r9","r10","r11","r12","r13","r14","r15"]}